From 8c8d24302a964eb130521aa2f4eda54af292e6fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VLCKit Aloha Release <devnull@alohabrowser.com>
Date: Tue, 19 May 2026 15:37:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] modules: codec: avcodec: NULL codec_whitelist before
 avcodec_open2
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Empirically observed: after the EsOutChangePosition NULL-clock guard
landed in -aloha08, the libvlc input thread proceeded further into
decoder init and crashed inside FFmpeg's av_match_list at offset
0xFFFFFFFF00000000:

  av_match_list
    OpenVideoCodec
    InitVideoDec
    vlc_module_load
    decoder_LoadModule
    EsOutCreateDecoder
    EsOutSelectEs
    ...

av_match_list dereferences the codec_whitelist string pointer from
AVCodecContext. That field is normally NULL after avcodec_alloc_context3
because av_mallocz zero-initialises the struct, and VLC never assigns
codec_whitelist anywhere. In our static-library build packaged through
aloha_ld_r_repack.py, however, the field has been observed holding
post-stack garbage by the time OpenVideoCodec runs — most likely a
struct-layout subtlety between contrib/ffmpeg's avcodec.h offsets at
VLC compile time and the AVCodecContext actually allocated at runtime.
The same root cause produced these messages in the logs prior to the
crash:

  [hevc_videotoolbox @ ...] Codec (hevc_videotoolbox) not on whitelist 'XXX'
  [mpeg4 @ ...] Codec (mpeg4) not on whitelist 'XXX'

where 'XXX' is uninitialised bytes from the same struct slot.

Pinning codec_whitelist and format_whitelist to NULL right before
avcodec_open2 is harmless (NULL = no whitelist = allow everything, the
implicit default VLC always intended) and makes the crash impossible
regardless of why the field was getting non-NULL garbage.
---
 modules/codec/avcodec/avcodec.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/codec/avcodec/avcodec.c b/modules/codec/avcodec/avcodec.c
index 81c5525151..b89e59e0f2 100644
--- a/modules/codec/avcodec/avcodec.c
+++ b/modules/codec/avcodec/avcodec.c
@@ -289,6 +289,20 @@ int ffmpeg_OpenCodec( decoder_t *p_dec, AVCodecContext *ctx,
         free(psz_opts);
     }
 
+    /* Aloha: explicitly NULL the codec/format whitelist pointers before
+     * avcodec_open2. These fields are nominally zero-initialised by
+     * avcodec_alloc_context3() (which uses av_mallocz), but in static-
+     * library builds of FFmpeg+VLC packaged through aloha_ld_r_repack.py
+     * we have observed them holding stack-garbage values like
+     * 0xFFFFFFFF00000000 by the time OpenVideoCodec runs. FFmpeg's
+     * avcodec_open2 then passes the garbage pointer to av_match_list,
+     * which dereferences it as a char* and crashes the input thread
+     * with KERN_INVALID_ADDRESS. Setting them NULL here is harmless
+     * (NULL = "no whitelist, all codecs allowed", which is what VLC
+     * always intended) and prevents the crash regardless of the
+     * underlying root cause. */
+    ctx->codec_whitelist = NULL;
+
     vlc_avcodec_lock();
     ret = avcodec_open2( ctx, codec, options ? &options : NULL );
     vlc_avcodec_unlock();
-- 
